Now we have 0.10 mol OH- left, and also we have 0.05 mol CH3COOH. The OH- will react with the weak acid: CH3COOH + OH- -> CH3COO- + H2O.
So we need to see how much OH- is consumed by acetic acid. Since OH- is 0.10 mol and acetic acid is 0.05 mol, the acetic acid will be completely neutralized, consuming 0.05 mol OH-, leaving 0.10 - 0.05 = 0.05 mol OH- excess. And we produce 0.05 mol acetate ion (CH3COO-). So after all reactions, we have:
