We are asked: "What is the diffusion coefficient for copper in aluminum at 600 degrees C? Preexponential and activation energy values for this system are 6.5 × 10^{-5} m^2/s and 136,000 J/mol, respectively." Choices are various numbers with exponents. We need to compute D = D0 * exp(-Q/(RT)). Temperature is 600°C, convert to Kelvin: 600 + 273 = 873 K. R = 8.314 J/(mol·K). Q = 136,000 J/mol. D0 = 6.5 × 10^{-5} m^2/s.

Compute exponent: -Q/(RT) = -136000/(8.314*873). Compute denominator: 8.314*873 = 8.314*800 = 6651.2, 8.314*73 = 606.922, total = 6651.2+606.922=7258.122. So exponent = -136000/7258.122 ≈ -18.74. More precisely: 136000/7258.122 = 18.74. So exp(-18.74) = ? Use calculator: exp(-18.74) = about 7.2e-9? Actually exp(-18.74) = 1/exp(18.74). exp(18.74) ≈ e^18.74. e^18 = 6.565e7, e^0.74 ≈ 2.096, product ~1.376e8, so reciprocal ~7.27e-9. Then D = 6.5e-5 * 7.27e-9 = 4.73e-13. That is about 4.7e-13. So answer J: 4.7 × 10^{-13} m^2/s. But check choices: J is "4. 7 \times1 0^{-1 3}" which is 4.7e-13. So answer J.

But let's compute more accurately: Q=136000, R=8.314, T=873. So Q/(RT)=136000/(8.314*873). Compute 8.314*873 = 8.314*870 = 7233.18, plus 8.314*3=24.942, total 7258.122. So 136000/7258.122 = 18.739. exp(-18.739)=? Using more precise: exp(-18.739)= 1/exp(18.739). exp(18.739)= exp(18)*exp(0.739). exp(18)=65659969.2, exp(0.739)=2.094, product ~1.375e8, reciprocal ~7.27e-9. Multiply by 6.5e-5 gives 4.73e-13. So indeed about 4.7e-13. So answer J.

Thus final answer: J.</think>The diffusion coefficient is calculated using the Arrhenius equation: \( D = D_0 \exp\left(-\frac{Q}{RT}\right) \). Given \( D_0 = 6.5 \times 10^{-5} \, \text{m}^2/\text{s} \), \( Q = 136,000 \, \text{J/mol} \), \( R = 8.314 \, \text{J/(mol·K)} \), and \( T = 600^\circ \text{C} = 873 \, \text{K} \), the exponent is \( -\frac{136,000}{8.314 \times 873} \approx -18.74 \). Thus, \( \exp(-18.74) \approx 7.27 \times 10^{-9} \), and \( D \approx 6.5 \times 10^{-5} \times 7.27 \times 10^{-9} = 4.73 \times 10^{-13} \, \text{m}^2/\text{s} \), which matches choice J.

