But let's double-check the translation: After the HA tag, we have "AAATGACTCTG..." We read AAA TGA CTC... So indeed AAA is Lys, TGA is stop. So the protein would be Met-Tyr-Pro-Tyr-Asp-Val-Pro-Asp-Tyr-Ala-Lys-stop. That is a very short peptide. So overexpression of the full-length GADD45G is not possible. So the reason is early termination.

Thus answer: A.</think>The sequence contains a premature stop codon (TGA) immediately after the HA tag, causing early translation termination and preventing expression of the full-length GADD45G protein.

