Second term: 1/(x(e^{2x}-1)) = 2x^2 / [2x^2 * x(e^{2x}-1)] = 2x^2 / [2x^3(e^{2x}-1)].
So sum = [ (x-1)x(e^{2x}-1) + 2x^2 ] / [2x^3(e^{2x}-1)] = x [ (x-1)(e^{2x}-1) + 2x ] / [2x^3(e^{2x}-1)] = [ (x-1)(e^{2x}-1) + 2x ] / [2x^2(e^{2x}-1)].

So L = lim_{x->0} [ (x-1)(e^{2x}-1) + 2x ] / [2x^2(e^{2x}-1)].

